const TERMS = {
 'PPAC':'Production Planning-Based Availability Check: checks supply and requirements in PP/DS. With SBC supply creation, it can plan missing supply; supported types also use product characteristics.',
 'CDP':'Characteristics-Dependent Planning: planning uses characteristic values to match a requirement with suitable supply. It needs the relevant characteristics, classes and integration in PP/DS.',
 'SBC':'Supply Creation-Based Confirmation: an aATP process that involves PP/DS when supply needs to be created. Its planning result helps establish a customer confirmation before physical production.',
 'IBP order-based supply planning':'Network supply planning using order-level demand and supply. It can create planned orders for an agreed handover to S/4; this is different from transferring forecast quantities as PIRs.',
 'Planning ownership':'The agreed system, material scope and horizon responsible for creating or changing supply. IBP and PP/DS must coordinate the same orders rather than each independently recreating them.',
 'Planned order':'A proposal to produce or procure a quantity on planned dates. It is a supply element, unlike a PIR (demand), and it is not physical inventory.',
 'Planning BOM':'A planning structure used to represent expected option or module usage. Attachment rates describe an expected mix; the customer configuration selects the actual manufacturing content.',
 'KMAT':'The configurable material representing the printer model. Characteristics define the customer’s chosen execution; it is not simply a fixed stock code.',
 'Class 300':'The class type used for variant configuration. It groups the characteristics that describe a configurable material.',
 '150% super-BOM':'All modelled component alternatives in one structure. Dependency logic selects the applicable content for a valid configuration.',
 '100% selected content':'The components and operations required for one configuration. This does not necessarily create a new independent BOM master.',
 'Super-routing':'A routing containing possible operations. Selection logic determines which operations apply to the configured product.',
 'Production version':'Manufacturing master data that links an applicable BOM and routing or recipe, subject to validity and lot-size ranges.',
 'PDS':'Production Data Structure: the manufacturing source used by PP/DS, derived from relevant production master data. The configurator alone is not the full source.',
 'PIR':'Planned Independent Requirement: a forecast-like operational demand object in S/4HANA. It is a demand element, not stock and not an IBP sales order.',
 'Attachment rate':'An expected proportion or usage of a module in the printer mix. In this illustrative design, planning owns the rates. It is not a rule proving a configuration is valid.',
 'Dependent requirement':'Component demand derived from a higher-level manufacturing requirement. A printer order for three units can ultimately require three print modules and 21 individual heads.',
 'Stock E':'Sales-order stock assigned to an individual sales order/item. It is different from freely interchangeable anonymous stock; common modules can still be planned collectively.',
 'Consumption':'Matching concrete requirements against eligible forecast requirements so the same demand is not planned twice. It is not a physical goods movement.',
 'Forecast reduction':'The withdrawal/fulfilment side of the forecast lifecycle. Goods-issue-related quantities must be retained appropriately so delivered demand does not reappear as unconsumed forecast.',
 'Goods receipt / GR':'Receipt of manufactured or purchased goods into inventory. Inspection or other restrictions may still prevent immediate use.',
 'Goods issue / GI':'Removal of stock, for example for production consumption or customer shipment. It differs from creating a requirement or consuming a forecast.',
 'PAL / BOP / ABC':'Product Allocation, Backorder Processing and Alternative-Based Confirmation: optional aATP capabilities with different jobs, not a mandatory sequence.',
 'MRP vs. PP/DS':'MRP focuses on requirements, quantities and basic dates. PP/DS provides detailed production planning and scheduling for its selected material/resource scope.',
 'pMRP':'Predictive Material and Resource Planning: a simulation capability for exploring demand and capacity, separate from the normal operational MRP run.'
};
